Keep VNC paint nodes on the primary plane

The VNC backend replaces the core assign_planes but only places the cursor. A paint node
that leaves the z-order (ANGI hides tiles in a hidden layer on workspace switches and
overlays) comes back with no plane, so the window is never drawn again. Restore the default.

--- a/libweston/backend-vnc/vnc.c
+++ b/libweston/backend-vnc/vnc.c
@@ -1084,9 +1084,19 @@
 vnc_output_assign_planes(struct weston_output *base)
 {
 	struct vnc_output *output = to_vnc_output(base);
+	struct weston_paint_node *pnode;
 
 	assert(output);
 
+	/* Replacing the core's default assign_planes also replaces its move of
+	 * every paint node to the primary plane. A view that left the z-order
+	 * (a hidden layer, an unmapped parent) returns with no plane and would
+	 * never be drawn again, so restore the default for all but the cursor. */
+	wl_list_for_each(pnode, &output->base.paint_node_z_order_list, z_order_link) {
+		if (pnode->plane != &output->cursor_plane)
+			weston_paint_node_move_to_plane(pnode, &output->base.primary_plane);
+	}
+
 	if (output->base.disable_planes)
 		return;
 
